Most players, when they first reach minetown, are not properly equipped to
handle the types of critters or traps that show up in Mines End.  I would
not go that way unless I had poison resistance, MR or at least searching,
a good lamp, and at least 2 escape/instakill methods of: jumping, fast
engraving, teleport, level teleport, very fast (speed boots or spell),
cursed gain level, genocide, wand/spell of death.

The main dungeon is much safer, at least for a few levels below Sokoban.
And the luckstone is nice, but not critical at this juncture of the game.
It's far more important to get a decent weapon, better armor, and a
just-plain-stronger character.

I typically take the following route:
- first level of the mines, if it's lit and I have use for metal armor, or
if gnomes or dwarves are peaceful
- Sokoban
- minetown
- main dungeon down to near the rogue level, or when I get MR / hitpoints
/ escape methods
- mines end

After this, Medusa or the Quest depending on equipment.  I often do all
but the last Quest level, to pick up as much equipment as possible, even
if I'm not ready for the nemesis.  After this, the equipment situation
always dictates my next move.



